        {
          "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
          "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued October 12 at 2:53PM PDT until October 13 at 3:00PM PDT by NWS San Francisco CA",
          "severity": "Minor",
          "urgency": "Expected",
          "description": "* WHAT...For the Coastal Flood Advisory, up to 1.4 ft of\ninundation above ground level is possible in low-lying areas\nnear shorelines and tidal waterways. For the Beach Hazards\nStatement, increased risk of rip currents and sneaker waves\nexpected with breaking waves up to 16 feet.\n\n* WHERE...San Francisco, Northern Monterey Bay and Southern\nMonterey Bay and Big Sur Coast Counties.\n\n* WHEN...For the Coastal Flood Advisory, until 3 PM PDT Tuesday.\nFor the Beach Hazards Statement, until 10 PM PDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of lots, parks, and roads with only\nisolated road closures expected. High tides will result in\nflooding along coastal trails, cut off access to some low-\nlying beaches and coastal areas, and bring water and waves\nfarther up the beach than typical. Dangerous conditions are\nforecast along the shoreline. Hazards include sneaker waves,\nstrong rip currents, and large breaking waves.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...At the San Francisco tidal gauge, high tide\nis expected to be 1.4 ft above normal (7.2 ft MLLW) at 1:14 PM\nTuesday 10/13. These predictions include up to 1.5 ft of surge\nthat will enhance the astronomical tide and flooding threat.\nHigh tide varies up to 90 minutes earlier or later along the\nPacific Coast and through the San Francisco Bay, respectively.",
          "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.\n\nStay off of jetties, piers, rocks, and other waterside\ninfrastructure. Remain out of the water to avoid hazardous surf\nand NEVER turn your back on the ocean. Monitor local weather,\nsurf and tide forecasts at www.weather.gov/mtr.",
          "expires": "2026-10-12T23:00:00-07:00",
          "source_url": "https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dca2b0ec93ebfe553cf1d84a27828385d114edb3.001.1"
        },
        {
          "event": "Beach Hazards Statement",
          "headline": "Beach Hazards Statement issued October 12 at 2:53PM PDT until October 12 at 10:00PM PDT by NWS San Francisco CA",
